    "The offer-level candidates separate an offer-wide promotional link from the existence of a non-discount gift component. They could catch an unrelated component unless the supplied facts establish that the gift itself has the required promotional connection.",
    "The fund-specific scope in several candidates is supported by the circular's context, but should not be treated as the complete scope of paragraph 3.11 across all investment products.",
    "A result under the selected gift control establishes neither compliance with disclosure and advertising duties nor compliance with section 103. The two claims assessed here do not supply additional gift exceptions or prohibitions.",
    "The supplied source does not establish an operative date interval. The temporal convention and conflict-handling semantics are implementation choices, not legal requirements stated in the quoted circular."
